<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="faq-section">
  <div class="faq-inner">
    <div class="faq-heading">
      <p>Common Questions</p>
      <h2>FAQ<em>s</em></h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item open">
      <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
        <h4>How long do repairs typically take?</h4>
        <div class="faq-toggle">+</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-answer">Most standard repairs — clasps, prongs, soldering — are completed within 3–5 business days. More complex work such as stone sourcing or full restorations may take 1–2 weeks. We'll always give you a timeframe upfront.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
        <h4>Can you resize any type of ring?</h4>
        <div class="faq-toggle">+</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-answer">We can resize most rings, including gold, silver, and rose gold bands. Some rings with full eternity settings or tension-set stones require special techniques — we'll advise you at consultation if there are any limitations.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
        <h4>How does the gold buying process work?</h4>
        <div class="faq-toggle">+</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-answer">Bring your gold jewellery into store — no appointment needed. We weigh and assess it on the spot, provide a transparent quote based on current market rates, and pay you same-day. There's no obligation to sell.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
        <h4>How long does a custom jewellery piece take?</h4>
        <div class="faq-toggle">+</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-answer">Custom pieces typically take 3–6 weeks from design approval to finished piece. We start with a consultation, move to CAD rendering for your approval, then into production. Rush timelines may be possible — contact us to discuss.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  function toggleFaq(btn) {
    var item = btn.closest('.faq-item');
    var isOpen = item.classList.contains('open');
    document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item.open').forEach(function(el) { el.classList.remove('open'); });
    if (!isOpen) item.classList.add('open');
  }
</script>

